  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nMainly dry weather, save for Sunday night through Monday across\nthe southern half of the region.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA slow moving upper trough is expected to head south through \nQuebec and across Long Island this weekend into early next week.\nFor the most part, our region will be within northwest flow \naround this system with surface high pressure over or near the \nregion. However, Sunday night into Monday, a cold front \nassociated with this low may bring some showers and storms to \nthe southern half of the region.\n\nFrom Tuesday through Friday, the trough to our east is expected to \nclose off and stall and/or shift east, all the while a surface ridge \nbuilds into the area from the west. This will keep us in a dry\npattern. However, building heights will yield milder\ntemperatures.\n\nTemperatures through the period are expected to be near or slightly \ncooler than normal through mid-week, then start increasing slowly \nthrough Friday.",
